      "title": "Notice of claim: 20 days",
      "narration": "Marcus breaks his wrist on March 1. The notice of claim provision requires him to tell the insurer within 20 days of the loss, or as soon as reasonably possible. Notice can be a phone call or a letter to the insurer or its authorized producer, and it need only identify the insured and the policy. Late notice does not defeat the claim if it was given as soon as reasonably possible. For disability income policies that pay for a long period, the insured may be required to give proof of continuing disability at reasonable intervals, usually every six months.",
