      "title": "Claim forms: 15 days",
      "narration": "Once the insurer receives notice, it must send Marcus the forms it wants used for proof of loss within 15 days. If the forms do not arrive in that time, Marcus may submit proof in any written form describing the occurrence, character and extent of the loss, and the insurer must accept it. The provision prevents an insurer from stalling a claim by withholding paperwork. In practice the clock runs from the insurer’s receipt of notice, and producers often help clients by supplying the forms directly.",
