      "title": "Prompt payment in Maryland",
      "text": "Maryland’s prompt payment statute requires insurers, nonprofit health service plans and HMOs to pay or send a status notice within 30 days of receiving a claim. Late payments on clean claims carry interest of 1.5 percent a month for days 31 to 60, 2 percent for days 61 to 120 and 2.5 percent after that, added automatically.",
